1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,610
For many time-poor, health-conscious people, the must-have kitchen gadget at the moment is an air fryer.
对于许多时间紧张、注重健康的人来说，当下厨房必备的小家电就是空气炸锅。

2
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:19,050
From top chefs to humble students, many are singing the praises of the device that seems to be flying off the shelves at shops and online.
从顶级大厨到普通学生，许多人都对这款设备赞不绝口，它在线上线下的商店里都卖得异常火爆。

3
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:26,060
One British department store reported sales increased by 400% in 2021.
英国一家百货公司报告称，2021年空气炸锅的销量涨幅高达400%。

4
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:33,280
But are they really the best thing since sliced bread, or is the hype all just hot air?!
但它们真的是继切片面包之后最棒的发明吗？还是说这场热度不过是夸夸其谈？

5
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:39,560
If you got one as a present, or bagged one in the sales, you'll already know the benefits.
如果你收到过一台空气炸锅作为礼物，或是在促销时入手了一台，那你一定已经知道它的好处。

6
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:46,070
An air fryer avoids the need to deep-fry food in hot and often unhealthy oil.
空气炸锅无需用滚烫且往往不健康的油来油炸食物。

7
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:55,180
Instead, the food is cooked by having very hot air blown on it at high speed – it doesn't actually fry but bakes the food.
相反，它是通过高速吹送热风来烹制食物——它实际上并非油炸，而是烘烤食物。

8
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:09,400
The technology sounds simple, and Dr Jakub Radzikowski, Culinary Education Designer at Imperial College London, told the BBC: "You could compare it to drying your hair with a hairdryer."
这项技术听起来十分简单，伦敦帝国理工学院的烹饪教育设计师雅各布·拉齐科夫斯基博士在接受BBC采访时表示：“你可以把它比作用吹风机吹头发。”

9
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:19,200
The combination of a powerful fan and a smaller compartment makes the air fryer more efficient and reduces the time needed to pre-heat it.
强劲的风扇和更小的腔体相结合，让空气炸锅的效率更高，还缩短了预热所需的时间。

10
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:26,600
In addition, because the food is cooked in a basket, excess fat will drip to the bottom, so you don't have to eat it.
此外，由于食物是放在炸篮中烹制的，多余的油脂会滴落到容器底部，你也就不会摄入这些油脂了。

11
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:35,415
And it's good to know air fryers use less energy than a conventional oven because of the shorter cooking times needed.
而且值得一提的是，由于烹制时间更短，空气炸锅比传统烤箱更省电。

12
00:01:35,415 --> 00:01:42,860
Some people may question how versatile they are and whether they can be used for cooking whole meals.
有些人可能会质疑它们的用途是否广泛，能不能用来做一整顿饭。

13
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:54,180
But experts have prepared crispy sweet potato fries, chips, and chicken and fish, quickly and with good flavoursome results – cooked to perfection.
但专家们已经用空气炸锅快速做出了酥脆的甜薯条、炸薯块、鸡肉和鱼肉，成品味道上佳，火候恰到好处。

14
00:01:54,180 --> 00:02:09,310
Dr Jakub Radzikowski's favourite is chicken legs or thighs, which he says after 20 minutes gives you something that's "perfectly juicy inside" with a skin that is so crispy it "shatters like glass".
雅各布·拉齐科夫斯基博士最爱的是用它做鸡腿或鸡大腿，他说，20分钟后，就能得到一份“内里汁水充盈”、外皮酥脆到“像玻璃一样一碰就碎”的成品。

15
00:02:09,310 --> 00:02:19,440
If this whets your appetite, remember that, because of the air fryer's size, there is a limit to the amount that can be cooked in them at one time.
如果这让你心动了，要记住，受限于空气炸锅的尺寸，它一次能烹制的食物量是有限的。

16
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,160
So your oven may still come in handy.
所以你的烤箱可能还是能派上用场。

17
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:31,800
But if you're on a budget or in a rush, it might be worth giving one a try and seeing what amazing meals you can serve up.
但如果你预算有限，或是时间紧张，不妨试试空气炸锅，看看能做出多少惊艳的美食。
